1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:25,025
>>>>>>>>>>>>Mr. -bu-1<<<<<<<<<<<<

2
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,406
Manuel.

3
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,449
Manuel!

4
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:11,715
Manuel.

5
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:46,935
I think....

6
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:51,147
I think I found you one.

7
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:57,487
Look, I called you, right?

8
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:03,576
Soon as I couldn't pull it out myself,
I called you, John.

9
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:20,885
It's okay, it's okay.
We had to tie her down, okay?

10
00:04:21,219 --> 00:04:22,846
It's okay.

11
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:16,441
This is Constantine.

12
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:21,529
John Constantine, asshole.

13
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,622
Sure.

14
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,812
What the hell?

15
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,038
I need a mirror.

16
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,208
Now. At least 3 feet high.

17
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:17,919
Move! Go, now!

18
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:33,143
This is Kramer.

19
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:36,563
Chas Kramer, asshole.

20
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,356
Asshole.

21
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:43,528
What? Oh, this is Kramer.
Chas Kramer, asshole.

22
00:06:43,695 --> 00:06:45,697
- Chas!
- What?

23
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:48,533
- Move the car.
- Why?

24
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:51,369
Move the damn car!

25
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:55,582
"Chas, move the car. "

26
00:06:57,709 --> 00:06:59,002
There, car's moved.

27
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:11,598
Lift it up over the bed.

28
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:17,437
Tie that end off.
Hennessy, over the top.

29
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:23,860
Close your eyes.
And whatever happens, don't look.

30
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,290
No!

31
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:45,340
Show yourself.

32
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,221
Smile pretty, you vain prick.

33
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,690
For your boss.

34
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:03,692
Pull it!

35
00:08:29,092 --> 00:08:30,927
Ma? Ma?

36
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:09,632
Like I said, I found you something,
didn't I, John? Didn't I?

37
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:11,384
What happened in there?

38
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,685
Going to a lot of meetings, I see.

39
00:09:20,852 --> 00:09:22,896
Keeps the voices out so I can sleep.

40
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,358
I have to sleep, John.

41
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:29,444
I need some help, Father.

42
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:31,654
You do?

43
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,490
From me?

44
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:35,283
What kind of-?

45
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:41,414
- Hey, listen, I-
- That exorcism wasn't right.

46
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:46,086
Listen to the ether.

47
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:50,465
Anything unusual, you let me know.

48
00:09:51,091 --> 00:09:55,804
Come on, you don't need its protection.
It'll be like back in the day.

49
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:00,934
A few days.

50
00:10:01,101 --> 00:10:02,394
Okay.

51
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,855
Okay. For you, John.

52
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:12,529
John, why would you do that
if you know it's not my car?

53
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,156
- I told you to move it.
- You did tell me to move it...

54
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:18,660
...but if you'd said you were dropping
a 300-pound mirror with a demon...

55
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:20,578
...I would've moved it further, John.

56
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:24,249
- Take Alvarado.
- Yeah, thank you. I know what to take.

57
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:29,129
You ever think if you told me more now
that maybe I could help out?

58
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:30,547
- No?
- Nope.

59
00:10:30,714 --> 00:10:32,007
Nope?

60
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:34,134
Of course it's a nope.

61
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:11,254
Bless me, Father, for I have sinned.

62
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,259
It's been...

63
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:20,305
...two weeks since my last confession.

64
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:25,643
I killed a man today.

65
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:28,313
Another one.

66
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:37,364
I didn't even see his face, I just...

67
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:40,617
...pulled the trigger, and he went away.

68
00:11:41,785 --> 00:11:47,707
Most cops go 20 years
without firing their guns.

69
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:52,754
Why do I always know
where these guys are?

70
00:11:52,921 --> 00:11:56,132
Where to aim, when to fire.

71
00:11:57,676 --> 00:12:00,512
I'm wondering, is there
something wrong with me, Father?

72
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:03,223
Something damned?

73
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:08,520
God has a plan for you.
He has a plan for us all.

74
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:12,899
You mustn't let your faith
be overshadowed by guilt.

75
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:15,026
Yeah, I'm trying.

76
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:18,154
I'm trying real hard.

77
00:12:19,698 --> 00:12:20,949
Isabel.

78
00:13:09,873 --> 00:13:12,000
Isabel.

79
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:08,515
Things I've beaten.

80
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:12,227
Things most people never even heard of.

81
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:15,689
And now I'm gonna be done in by this.

82
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:18,983
Wouldn't be the first, John.

83
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:22,737
Come on, Les.

84
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:25,156
You saved me before,
you can do it again, right?

85
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:28,076
This is aggressive.

86
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:32,163
Twenty years ago,
you didn't wanna be here.

87
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,208
Now you don't wanna leave.

88
00:14:35,834 --> 00:14:37,919
Yeah, that's a good idea.

89
00:14:40,755 --> 00:14:42,674
John, you really need to prepare.

90
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:49,931
- Make arrangements.
- No need.

91
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:53,101
I already know exactly where I'm going.

92
00:14:57,022 --> 00:14:58,857
- Morning.
- Good morning.

93
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:01,818
- Good morning.
- Detective.

94
00:15:01,985 --> 00:15:03,737
- No, no, no.
- Angela, wait.

95
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:06,489
You don't need to see this, okay? No.

96
00:15:07,574 --> 00:15:09,034
Give us the room, please.

97
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:40,940
Isabel.

98
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,574
She fell from the roof?

99
00:15:49,741 --> 00:15:51,493
She jumped.

100
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,121
- No.
- Look...

101
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:59,292
...I know it's hard to accept.
She was sick.

102
00:16:07,425 --> 00:16:10,845
- Isabel wouldn't kill herself.
- Angie.

103
00:16:11,429 --> 00:16:13,431
- She wouldn't kill herself.
- Detective.

104
00:16:13,598 --> 00:16:14,891
- Period.
- Detective.

105
00:16:15,058 --> 00:16:16,601
Period!

106
00:16:17,352 --> 00:16:21,147
Angie, there were security cameras.

107
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:33,451
- Hold the door. You going down?
- Not if I can help it.

108
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:23,585
A new case?

109
00:17:24,085 --> 00:17:29,299
The big score? The mother lode?
The one you've been waiting for?

110
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:32,344
- Humor me.
- Don't I always?

111
00:17:37,182 --> 00:17:40,602
Oh, yeah, that's-
Much obliged. Thank you.

112
00:17:42,479 --> 00:17:44,147
How you feeling, John?

113
00:17:44,397 --> 00:17:45,899
So, what's new?

114
00:17:50,028 --> 00:17:53,615
Bullet shavings from
the assassination attempt on the pope...

115
00:17:53,782 --> 00:17:57,285
...holy-water ampoules
from the River Jordan...

116
00:17:57,452 --> 00:18:02,165
...and- Oh, you'll love this.
- screech beetle from Amityville.

117
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:08,171
Yeah, it's funny to you, but to the
fallen, that's like nails on a chalkboard.

118
00:18:08,338 --> 00:18:11,299
What is it, exactly, with you and bugs?

119
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:14,260
I just like them.

120
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:16,221
Yeah. Who doesn't?

121
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:20,266
Yeah, easy there, hero.

122
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:23,895
- That's dragon's breath.
- I thought you couldn't get it anymore.

123
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:28,650
Yeah, well, I know a guy
who knows a guy.

124
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:37,992
So, what's the action?

125
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:42,080
I just pulled a soldier demon
out of a little girl.

126
00:18:42,497 --> 00:18:45,208
Looked like it was trying
to come through.

127
00:18:46,835 --> 00:18:48,128
Yeah, I know how it sounds.

128
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,463
No, we're finger puppets
to them, John...

129
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:51,965
...not doorways.

130
00:18:52,132 --> 00:18:56,052
They can work us, but they can't
come through onto our plane.

131
00:18:56,219 --> 00:18:58,722
Check the scrolls anyway.
See if there's any precedent.

132
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:00,724
Sure thing, John.

133
00:19:01,766 --> 00:19:03,351
Anything else?

134
00:19:03,518 --> 00:19:06,438
Wouldn't happen to have
anything for a-?

135
00:19:08,023 --> 00:19:09,315
On the house.

136
00:19:10,025 --> 00:19:13,653
All right, question. How much longer
do I have to be your slave, John?

137
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:17,615
You're not my slave, Chas.

138
00:19:18,408 --> 00:19:21,327
You're my very appreciated apprentice.

139
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:23,538
Like Tonto or Robin.

140
00:19:23,997 --> 00:19:26,291
Or that skinny fellow
with the fat friend.

141
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:30,170
Right. So then why don't I apprentice
something besides driving, then, John?

142
00:19:32,964 --> 00:19:34,591
John? John.

143
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:38,345
I love our little talks, John.

144
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:53,151
May I take your coat, Mr. Constantine?

145
00:19:53,318 --> 00:19:55,987
No, thanks,
I'm not gonna be staying long.

146
00:19:56,154 --> 00:20:00,533
- How about you, ma'am?
- Oh, no, I'm not staying long either.

147
00:20:00,909 --> 00:20:03,119
I really need to speak with him.
It's important.

148
00:20:03,286 --> 00:20:05,872
First come, first served.

149
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:11,878
So you're rude no matter where you are.

150
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:22,055
- Father.
- Hi.

151
00:20:23,056 --> 00:20:26,142
- You have news. Yes.
- Yes, I spoke with the bishop.

152
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,484
I know what you want, son.

153
00:20:34,651 --> 00:20:38,029
Still keeping your all-seeing eye
on me, Gabriel?

154
00:20:39,489 --> 00:20:41,491
I'm flattered.

155
00:20:42,659 --> 00:20:44,744
Well, I could offer something...

156
00:20:44,911 --> 00:20:48,998
...about how a shepherd leads
even the most wayward of his flock...

157
00:20:49,332 --> 00:20:51,167
...but it might sound disingenuous.

158
00:20:51,334 --> 00:20:53,962
She has to have a Catholic funeral,
Father. She has to.

159
00:20:54,129 --> 00:20:58,174
- Angela, it's still considered a mortal sin.
- She didn't commit suicide.

160
00:20:58,299 --> 00:21:00,844
The bishop believes otherwise.
You know the rules.

161
00:21:01,011 --> 00:21:02,971
Oh, rules.

162
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:04,931
Father.

163
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:06,599
David.

164
00:21:08,059 --> 00:21:10,020
This is Isabel.

165
00:21:10,186 --> 00:21:13,815
God was the only one
she ever believed loved her.

166
00:21:14,733 --> 00:21:16,317
Please.

167
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,778
I'm sorry.

168
00:21:21,573 --> 00:21:24,868
I've been seeing some unusual
soul traffic lately.

169
00:21:25,035 --> 00:21:27,662
You might consider
giving me an extension.

170
00:21:27,829 --> 00:21:30,290
I could do your side some good
these days.

171
00:21:30,498 --> 00:21:32,625
You still trying to buy your way
into heaven?

172
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:36,379
What about the minions I've sent back?

173
00:21:36,546 --> 00:21:40,550
- That alone should guarantee my entry.
- How many times have I told you?

174
00:21:40,717 --> 00:21:42,635
That's not the way this works.

175
00:21:42,802 --> 00:21:45,388
Why, haven't I served him enough?

176
00:21:46,348 --> 00:21:49,142
- What does he want from me?
- Only the usual.

177
00:21:49,309 --> 00:21:52,270
Self-sacrifice, belief.

178
00:21:52,437 --> 00:21:55,523
- Oh, I believe, for chrissake.
- No, no, you know.

179
00:21:55,690 --> 00:21:57,817
And there's a difference. You've seen.

180
00:21:57,984 --> 00:22:02,489
I never asked to see.
I was born with this curse.

181
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:04,616
A gift, John.

182
00:22:04,783 --> 00:22:07,202
One that you've squandered
on selfish endeavors.

183
00:22:07,369 --> 00:22:10,747
I'm pulling demons out of little girls.

184
00:22:10,914 --> 00:22:12,665
Who's that for?

185
00:22:13,625 --> 00:22:17,170
Everything you've ever done,
you've only ever done for yourself.

186
00:22:17,379 --> 00:22:19,506
To earn your way
back into his good graces.

187
00:22:19,673 --> 00:22:22,175
Impossible rules, endless regulations...

188
00:22:22,342 --> 00:22:26,304
...who goes up, who goes down
and why.

189
00:22:30,475 --> 00:22:33,103
You don't even understand us.

190
00:22:33,770 --> 00:22:36,272
You're the one who should go
to hell, half-breed.

191
00:22:48,535 --> 00:22:50,412
Why me, Gabriel?

192
00:22:51,746 --> 00:22:54,082
It's personal, isn't it?

193
00:22:54,582 --> 00:22:59,713
I didn't go to church enough,
I didn't pray enough...

194
00:23:00,046 --> 00:23:04,175
...I was 5 bucks short
in the collection plate. Why?

195
00:23:06,094 --> 00:23:08,722
You are going to die young...

196
00:23:08,888 --> 00:23:12,642
...because you smoked 30 cigarettes
a day since you were 15.

197
00:23:13,143 --> 00:23:15,562
And you're going to go to hell...

198
00:23:15,979 --> 00:23:18,648
...because of the life you took.

199
00:23:23,486 --> 00:23:25,238
You're fucked.

200
00:23:36,458 --> 00:23:38,710
At least it's nice out.

201
00:23:41,212 --> 00:23:44,341
He always had a rotten sense of humor.

202
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:53,183
And his punch lines are killers.

203
00:23:59,105 --> 00:24:00,565
John!

204
00:24:00,982 --> 00:24:04,694
Constantine, it's raining! John! Hey!

205
00:24:16,539 --> 00:24:20,251
Twenty-two women were found buried
in the assailant's back yard.

206
00:24:20,418 --> 00:24:23,963
So much damage had been done
to the bodies, police had to match...

207
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:26,466
Police report she had been
physically penetrated...

208
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:29,260
...over 100 times and buried alive.

209
00:24:29,427 --> 00:24:33,014
- found locked in a storage freezer,
his head severed and his organs...

210
00:24:33,181 --> 00:24:34,933
He stuffed Holly's body into...

211
00:24:35,100 --> 00:24:38,895
- The bodies ravished by the unknown...
- He used a small handsaw...

212
00:24:39,062 --> 00:24:42,399
Had nearly decapitated...
Even his eyes were gouged out.

213
00:24:42,565 --> 00:24:44,150
Isabel.

214
00:25:07,048 --> 00:25:09,175
I'm so sorry, Izzy.

215
00:25:09,718 --> 00:25:11,302
Constantine.

216
00:25:44,044 --> 00:25:45,837
Dodson.

217
00:25:46,129 --> 00:25:47,714
Hello?

218
00:25:48,465 --> 00:25:50,091
Hello.

219
00:25:55,430 --> 00:25:57,015
Hello?

220
00:26:56,825 --> 00:26:59,786
Hey. Hey, buddy, got a light?

221
00:27:29,691 --> 00:27:33,528
Should've minded
your own business, exorcist.

222
00:27:54,716 --> 00:27:58,636
I know where you're going, John.
You're going to Midnite's.

223
00:27:58,803 --> 00:28:00,388
You're supposed to wait in the cab.

224
00:28:00,555 --> 00:28:04,184
It's a haven for those who rise and fall.
I remember reading about this, John.

225
00:28:04,351 --> 00:28:06,978
- You read too much, kid. It's a bar.
- It's a bar?

226
00:28:07,145 --> 00:28:11,358
It's a bar. Papa Midnite is a crusader for
good. He swore the oath of neutrality.

227
00:28:11,524 --> 00:28:14,027
- John, the man's a legend.
- Yeah.

228
00:28:14,194 --> 00:28:16,571
Can you please get me
into this bar, John, please?

229
00:28:16,780 --> 00:28:18,239
I'm begging you, John, please?

230
00:28:19,074 --> 00:28:21,451
- Sure, you can get in.
- I can get in?

231
00:28:21,618 --> 00:28:23,703
If you can get in.

232
00:28:24,245 --> 00:28:27,999
If I can get-? It's a bear, though, right?
Or two ducks in a cloud?

233
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:33,505
Two frogs on a bench.

234
00:28:37,842 --> 00:28:39,552
Two frogs on a bench.

235
00:28:39,719 --> 00:28:41,638
No, no, I'm with the guy you just-

236
00:28:41,805 --> 00:28:43,598
John! John!

237
00:28:43,765 --> 00:28:45,684
I'm with him, though.

238
00:28:46,768 --> 00:28:48,645
Rat in a dress.

239
00:28:49,437 --> 00:28:52,023
Of course it is. Rat in a dress.

240
00:28:52,190 --> 00:28:54,067
I'm just testing. I'm just testing.

241
00:29:46,161 --> 00:29:47,912
Don't get up.

242
00:29:48,997 --> 00:29:51,416
You've been absent some time.

243
00:29:51,624 --> 00:29:54,461
Have you come here with relics to sell?

244
00:29:54,836 --> 00:29:57,922
No, I'm out of that now.
I've been too busy.

245
00:29:58,757 --> 00:30:01,801
Perhaps peddling forgeries has ended up
being bad for your health.

246
00:30:01,968 --> 00:30:03,845
Midnite, Jesus...

247
00:30:04,012 --> 00:30:07,265
...I thought the thing was authentic.

248
00:30:10,060 --> 00:30:11,728
I see now.

249
00:30:11,895 --> 00:30:15,065
Your health is bad for other reasons.
How long?

250
00:30:15,231 --> 00:30:16,941
A few months, maybe a year.

251
00:30:17,108 --> 00:30:19,694
I thought I heard thunder last night.

252
00:30:19,903 --> 00:30:22,822
Must have been
Satan's stomach growling.

253
00:30:24,324 --> 00:30:26,951
You're the one soul he'd come
up here himself to collect.

254
00:30:27,118 --> 00:30:29,329
So I've heard.

255
00:30:30,121 --> 00:30:32,665
Well, I am most certain
you did not come here...

256
00:30:32,832 --> 00:30:35,877
...for a sympathetic shoulder
to cry on.

257
00:30:38,338 --> 00:30:41,716
A demon just attacked me,
right out in the open on Figueroa.

258
00:30:42,008 --> 00:30:44,052
They don't like you, John.

259
00:30:44,219 --> 00:30:46,012
How many have you
deported back to hell?

260
00:30:46,179 --> 00:30:50,517
Not some angry half-breed, Midnite.
A full-fledged demon, here, on our plane.

261
00:30:50,684 --> 00:30:53,311
Clearly I do not have to remind you
that is impossible.

262
00:30:53,478 --> 00:30:55,730
And yesterday I saw a soldier demon...

263
00:30:55,897 --> 00:30:58,274
...trying to chew its way out
through a little girl.

264
00:30:58,441 --> 00:31:02,987
Listen, John, demons stay in hell,
angels in heaven...

265
00:31:03,154 --> 00:31:05,573
...the great détente
of the original superpowers.

266
00:31:05,782 --> 00:31:10,495
Thanks for the history lesson, Midnite.
You've been a tremendous help.

267
00:31:10,620 --> 00:31:12,163
Now...

268
00:31:14,249 --> 00:31:15,625
...I need to use the chair.

269
00:31:18,628 --> 00:31:23,091
John, forgetting the fact that it would
almost certainly kill you...

270
00:31:23,299 --> 00:31:24,926
...you know I am neutral.

271
00:31:25,093 --> 00:31:29,139
And as long as the balance
is maintained, I take no sides.

272
00:31:29,639 --> 00:31:32,809
Before you were a bartender...

273
00:31:33,351 --> 00:31:37,147
...you were one witch doctor
against, what, 30 Ashgar?

274
00:31:37,981 --> 00:31:40,859
- And I-
- You were Constantine.

275
00:31:41,526 --> 00:31:44,279
The John Constantine.

276
00:31:45,030 --> 00:31:46,614
Once.

277
00:31:47,907 --> 00:31:51,202
This isn't the usual game, I can feel it.

278
00:31:51,369 --> 00:31:53,663
Something's coming.

279
00:31:54,497 --> 00:31:56,374
Spooky.

280
00:31:56,541 --> 00:31:58,293
Balthazar.

281
00:31:58,460 --> 00:32:02,339
That expression alone
has made my entire night.

282
00:32:02,881 --> 00:32:04,382
I'll make your night.

283
00:32:04,549 --> 00:32:08,094
I'll deport your sorry ass right where
you stand, you half-breed shit!

284
00:32:09,637 --> 00:32:14,351
You know the rules of my house.
While here, you will abide by them.

285
00:32:14,517 --> 00:32:16,394
Johnny boy.

286
00:32:18,772 --> 00:32:22,817
Word is you're on your way down.

287
00:32:23,109 --> 00:32:25,070
Fresh meat.

288
00:32:28,406 --> 00:32:30,450
Finger-licking good.

289
00:32:30,950 --> 00:32:32,535
We have a meeting now, John.

290
00:32:40,293 --> 00:32:42,420
What? I didn't catch that.

291
00:33:24,087 --> 00:33:26,339
Welcome to my life.

292
00:33:35,515 --> 00:33:36,808
Mr. Constantine.

293
00:33:39,019 --> 00:33:41,146
- I saw you-
- I remember.

294
00:33:41,688 --> 00:33:44,649
- And then I saw you at the-
- Regular kismet.

295
00:33:45,817 --> 00:33:49,154
I'd like to ask you a few questions,
if that would be okay.

296
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:52,282
I'm not really in the talking mood
right now.

297
00:33:52,699 --> 00:33:54,993
Well, maybe you could just listen then.

298
00:33:55,618 --> 00:33:57,203
Please?

299
00:34:01,207 --> 00:34:02,751
Always a catch.

300
00:34:17,015 --> 00:34:19,601
My sister was murdered yesterday.

301
00:34:19,768 --> 00:34:22,604
- Sorry to hear.
- Thanks.

302
00:34:22,979 --> 00:34:27,650
She was a patient at Ravenscar.
She jumped off the roof.

303
00:34:28,276 --> 00:34:30,153
Thought you said she was murdered.

304
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:33,198
Yeah, well, Isabel wouldn't
have taken her own life.

305
00:34:33,365 --> 00:34:36,868
Yeah, what kind of mental patient
kills herself?

306
00:34:37,660 --> 00:34:39,829
That's just crazy.

307
00:34:43,583 --> 00:34:47,379
Look, I've heard your name
around the precinct.

308
00:34:47,545 --> 00:34:52,550
I know the circles you travel in.
The occult, demonology, exorcisms.

309
00:34:52,717 --> 00:34:56,179
Just before my sister was committed,
she became deeply paranoid.

310
00:34:56,346 --> 00:35:00,892
She started talking about demons,
angels.

311
00:35:01,059 --> 00:35:03,687
Now, I think someone got to her,
Mr. Constantine.

312
00:35:03,853 --> 00:35:07,482
I think they brainwashed her
into stepping off that roof.

313
00:35:07,649 --> 00:35:11,903
Some kind of legion or cult.

314
00:35:12,195 --> 00:35:14,906
Sounds like a theory, detective.

315
00:35:15,073 --> 00:35:16,449
Good luck.

316
00:35:18,660 --> 00:35:21,121
I thought with your background,
you could at least...

317
00:35:21,287 --> 00:35:22,872
...point me in the right direction.

318
00:35:23,039 --> 00:35:25,250
Yeah, okay, sure.

319
00:35:28,420 --> 00:35:30,380
It wasn't a suicide.

320
00:35:30,547 --> 00:35:32,632
My sister was a devout Catholic.

321
00:35:32,799 --> 00:35:35,176
Do you understand that?
If she took her own life-

322
00:35:35,343 --> 00:35:38,013
Her soul would go straight to hell...

323
00:35:38,179 --> 00:35:43,101
...where she'd be ripped apart over
and over in screaming, brutal agony...

324
00:35:43,268 --> 00:35:46,396
...for all eternity. That it?

325
00:35:46,563 --> 00:35:48,523
That about right?

326
00:35:55,196 --> 00:35:57,240
Goddamn you.

327
00:36:26,311 --> 00:36:27,771
Detective.

328
00:36:27,937 --> 00:36:30,648
What if I told you that God
and the devil made a wager...

329
00:36:30,815 --> 00:36:34,152
...a kind of standing bet
for the souls of all mankind?

330
00:36:34,319 --> 00:36:36,696
I'd tell you to stay on your meds.

331
00:36:36,863 --> 00:36:40,992
Humor me. No direct contact with
humans. That would be the rule.

332
00:36:41,326 --> 00:36:45,372
- Just influence. See who would win.
- Okay, I'm humoring you.

333
00:36:45,538 --> 00:36:47,499
- Why?
- Who knows.

334
00:36:47,665 --> 00:36:50,627
- Maybe just for the fun of it. No telling.
- Oh, so it's fun.

335
00:36:50,794 --> 00:36:55,590
It's fun when a man beats his wife to
death, when a mother drowns her baby.

336
00:36:55,757 --> 00:36:59,344
And you think the devil is responsible?

337
00:36:59,511 --> 00:37:02,138
People are evil, Mr. Constantine. People.

338
00:37:02,305 --> 00:37:05,642
You're right. We're born
capable of terrible things.

339
00:37:05,809 --> 00:37:09,396
Then sometimes something else comes
along and gives us just the right nudge.

340
00:37:09,562 --> 00:37:12,857
Well, this has been real educational...

341
00:37:13,024 --> 00:37:14,693
...but I don't believe in the devil.

342
00:37:14,859 --> 00:37:18,154
You should. He believes in you.

343
00:37:37,465 --> 00:37:39,592
It's a power outage.

344
00:37:39,759 --> 00:37:41,636
Not likely.

345
00:37:44,180 --> 00:37:47,434
- What?
- We should go. Now.

346
00:37:52,355 --> 00:37:54,274
What is that?

347
00:37:55,316 --> 00:37:56,985
Wings.

348
00:37:57,527 --> 00:37:59,779
Maybe talons.

349
00:38:00,113 --> 00:38:02,699
You're kidding. Of what?

350
00:38:03,700 --> 00:38:06,578
Something that's not
supposed to be here.

351
00:38:10,331 --> 00:38:12,834
That's really not going to help.

352
00:38:17,255 --> 00:38:19,799
- Close your eyes.
- Why?

353
00:38:19,966 --> 00:38:21,217
Suit yourself.

354
00:38:42,781 --> 00:38:45,825
Demons stay in hell, huh?

355
00:38:47,118 --> 00:38:49,120
Tell them that.

356
00:38:51,164 --> 00:38:55,835
Don't worry. Happens to everyone
the first time.

357
00:38:56,086 --> 00:38:58,046
It's the sulfur.

358
00:38:58,588 --> 00:39:00,507
Sulfur.

359
00:39:02,634 --> 00:39:04,928
What were those things?

360
00:39:06,179 --> 00:39:07,889
Demons.

361
00:39:09,516 --> 00:39:13,812
- Scavengers of the damned.
- No, no. It's impossible.

362
00:39:14,020 --> 00:39:17,649
Yeah. And I don't think
they were after me.

363
00:39:19,693 --> 00:39:22,612
You really believe
she wouldn't commit suicide.

364
00:39:22,779 --> 00:39:24,114
Isabel?

365
00:39:24,864 --> 00:39:26,866
Never in a million years.

366
00:39:27,242 --> 00:39:29,244
Well, let's be sure.

367
00:39:29,452 --> 00:39:31,830
Let's see if she's in hell.

368
00:39:55,228 --> 00:39:57,397
Oh, was it supposed to be hot or cold?

369
00:39:57,856 --> 00:39:59,899
In front of the chair.

370
00:40:02,694 --> 00:40:04,446
I can't believe I'm doing this.

371
00:40:04,612 --> 00:40:07,115
- These are all Isabel's things?
- Yeah.

372
00:40:08,283 --> 00:40:10,035
- How about the cat?
- Duck?

373
00:40:10,785 --> 00:40:12,704
Yeah, why?

374
00:40:13,705 --> 00:40:14,998
Duck.

375
00:40:15,165 --> 00:40:17,375
Oh, you think that's strange.

376
00:40:17,542 --> 00:40:18,960
Cats are good.

377
00:40:19,127 --> 00:40:20,670
Half in, half out anyway.

378
00:40:38,229 --> 00:40:41,316
If this is some kind of spell
or something...

379
00:40:41,483 --> 00:40:44,527
...don't you need candles
and a pentagram for it to work?

380
00:40:44,694 --> 00:40:46,905
Why, do you have any?

381
00:40:47,197 --> 00:40:50,033
- This is crazy.
- Yes.

382
00:40:53,411 --> 00:40:55,663
I need you to leave.

383
00:40:56,498 --> 00:40:59,209
- I'm sorry?
- Angela, please.

384
00:41:03,338 --> 00:41:05,215
The apartment.

385
00:41:07,175 --> 00:41:08,927
Okay.

386
00:41:15,016 --> 00:41:17,435
Be careful with that cat.

387
00:41:21,398 --> 00:41:23,983
God, I hate this part.

388
00:43:21,810 --> 00:43:24,479
- Isabel.
- Constantine.

389
00:44:08,148 --> 00:44:09,524
Angela.

390
00:44:12,819 --> 00:44:14,320
Jesus.

391
00:44:18,366 --> 00:44:20,035
- Constantine, what-?
- Twins.

392
00:44:20,201 --> 00:44:22,037
Jesus. What?

393
00:44:22,912 --> 00:44:25,290
- You were twins.
- What did you say?

394
00:44:25,498 --> 00:44:28,043
- She killed herself.
- What?

395
00:44:29,127 --> 00:44:31,629
And she's damned for it.

396
00:44:44,100 --> 00:44:45,769
How is this possible?

397
00:44:48,188 --> 00:44:49,939
I need to eat.

398
00:46:33,376 --> 00:46:35,670
Hey! Hey, what are you doing in here?

399
00:46:38,631 --> 00:46:40,383
Relax, man.

400
00:46:40,967 --> 00:46:42,719
Slow down!

401
00:47:04,991 --> 00:47:07,786
What the hell kind of place is this?

402
00:47:56,334 --> 00:47:58,044
John.

403
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:30,952
When I was a kid, I could see things.

404
00:48:31,453 --> 00:48:33,413
Things humans aren't supposed to see.

405
00:48:34,914 --> 00:48:37,667
Things you shouldn't have to see.

406
00:48:54,559 --> 00:48:58,688
My parents were normal.
They did what most parents would do.

407
00:48:58,897 --> 00:49:01,232
They made it worse.

408
00:49:03,610 --> 00:49:06,279
You think you're crazy long enough...

409
00:49:06,738 --> 00:49:07,989
...you find a way out.

410
00:49:08,406 --> 00:49:12,077
- You tried to kill yourself.
- I didn't try anything.

411
00:49:15,705 --> 00:49:18,667
Officially, I was dead for two minutes.

412
00:49:19,501 --> 00:49:21,836
But when you cross over...

413
00:49:22,962 --> 00:49:25,173
...time stops.

414
00:49:26,549 --> 00:49:29,302
Take it from me,
two minutes in hell is a lifetime.

415
00:49:31,179 --> 00:49:33,348
When I came back...

416
00:49:35,183 --> 00:49:36,935
...I knew...

417
00:49:37,227 --> 00:49:39,896
...all the things I could see were real.

418
00:49:41,147 --> 00:49:46,069
Heaven and hell are right here.
Behind every wall, every window.

419
00:49:46,236 --> 00:49:51,032
The world behind the world,
and we're smack in the middle.

420
00:49:51,282 --> 00:49:54,577
Angels and demons can't
cross over onto our plane.

421
00:49:54,744 --> 00:49:57,539
So instead we get
what I call half-breeds.

422
00:49:58,623 --> 00:50:00,792
The influence peddlers.

423
00:50:00,959 --> 00:50:06,172
They can only whisper in our ears, but
a single word can give you courage...

424
00:50:06,339 --> 00:50:10,218
...or turn your favorite pleasure
into your worst nightmare.

425
00:50:10,385 --> 00:50:13,304
Those with the demon's touch...

426
00:50:13,471 --> 00:50:18,309
...like those part angel,
living alongside us.

427
00:50:18,476 --> 00:50:20,854
They call it the balance.

428
00:50:21,271 --> 00:50:24,274
I call it hypocritical bullshit.

429
00:50:25,775 --> 00:50:28,236
So when a half-breed breaks the rules...

430
00:50:28,737 --> 00:50:32,490
...I deport their sorry ass
straight back to hell.

431
00:50:33,116 --> 00:50:35,618
I don't get them all...

432
00:50:36,745 --> 00:50:39,914
...but I've been hoping to get enough
to ensure my...

433
00:50:40,874 --> 00:50:43,752
- ...retirement.
- I don't understand.

434
00:50:45,628 --> 00:50:47,756
I'm a suicide, Angela.

435
00:50:47,922 --> 00:50:51,301
When I die, the rules say
I've got just one place to go.

436
00:50:51,468 --> 00:50:53,428
You're trying to buy your way
into heaven.

437
00:50:53,595 --> 00:50:56,014
What would you do
if you were sentenced to a prison...

438
00:50:56,181 --> 00:50:58,433
...where half the inmates
were put there by you?

439
00:51:00,727 --> 00:51:03,146
I guess God has a plan for all of us.

440
00:51:03,563 --> 00:51:06,566
God's a kid with an ant farm, lady.

441
00:51:06,733 --> 00:51:08,693
He's not planning anything.

442
00:51:09,027 --> 00:51:10,945
When we were little...

443
00:51:11,905 --> 00:51:14,407
...Isabel saw things too.

444
00:51:19,579 --> 00:51:20,955
Dodson.

445
00:51:23,458 --> 00:51:26,795
Guard spotted him groping the body,
then he ran across the street.

446
00:51:26,961 --> 00:51:29,923
Came in here, and he had a go
at the entire stock.

447
00:51:30,090 --> 00:51:33,176
He drowned himself in alcohol
in under a minute.

448
00:51:33,760 --> 00:51:36,262
Could've been a member
of my fraternity.

449
00:51:38,640 --> 00:51:40,517
Hey, what the hell is he doing here?

450
00:51:40,809 --> 00:51:42,227
He's okay.

451
00:51:51,319 --> 00:51:54,781
Why didn't you call me,
you son of a bitch?

452
00:52:28,106 --> 00:52:29,691
Yes?

453
00:52:30,775 --> 00:52:32,360
What do you mean?

454
00:52:33,236 --> 00:52:34,654
What?

455
00:52:34,821 --> 00:52:36,322
How?

456
00:52:47,375 --> 00:52:50,337
Got it. Bye.

457
00:52:56,593 --> 00:52:59,471
I need to see where Isabel died.

458
00:52:59,637 --> 00:53:02,682
Séances, Ouija boards, channeling.

459
00:53:03,266 --> 00:53:06,728
Our father thought she was
just trying to get attention.

460
00:53:06,978 --> 00:53:09,314
She certainly did that.

461
00:53:09,522 --> 00:53:12,859
She'd tell everyone about the things
she said she saw.

462
00:53:13,026 --> 00:53:16,571
She'd scare my mother half to death.

463
00:53:18,323 --> 00:53:20,867
And then she stopped talking
for almost a year.

464
00:53:21,034 --> 00:53:23,203
So you had her committed.

465
00:53:23,370 --> 00:53:24,621
Yeah.

466
00:53:24,788 --> 00:53:26,373
How long?

467
00:53:26,748 --> 00:53:28,416
Two weeks.

468
00:53:28,875 --> 00:53:30,543
This time.

469
00:53:30,710 --> 00:53:35,131
She'd get better, and then she'd
get worse. Recently, a lot worse.

470
00:53:37,050 --> 00:53:40,512
That symbol that was cut
in the dead guy's hand...

471
00:53:40,679 --> 00:53:42,889
...does it have something to do
with this?

472
00:53:43,181 --> 00:53:45,350
I'm a cop, John, remember?

473
00:53:45,517 --> 00:53:50,271
You don't walk off the roof of a building
without leaving something behind.

474
00:53:50,438 --> 00:53:55,110
And I showed you everything
she left behind in that box, but feel free.

475
00:53:55,276 --> 00:54:00,407
Maybe she left something else.
Not something a cop would find.

476
00:54:01,825 --> 00:54:03,576
Something just for you.

477
00:54:05,036 --> 00:54:09,082
You were her twin, Angela.
Twins tend to think alike.

478
00:54:09,249 --> 00:54:12,419
- I'm not like my sister.
- But you were once.

479
00:54:12,585 --> 00:54:14,713
When you were kids.

480
00:54:15,046 --> 00:54:17,674
When you'd spend every second
with each other.

481
00:54:17,841 --> 00:54:21,428
You'd start a sentence, she'd finish it.
You'd get hurt, she'd cry.

482
00:54:21,594 --> 00:54:23,013
That was a long time ago.

483
00:54:23,179 --> 00:54:25,056
That kind of bond doesn't
just disappear.

484
00:54:25,181 --> 00:54:27,183
There is nothing here.

485
00:54:27,767 --> 00:54:30,812
- Hey. Come on.
- She planned her death in this room.

486
00:54:30,979 --> 00:54:34,232
She thought it up right here.
Right where you're standing.

487
00:54:34,399 --> 00:54:37,527
She knew you'd come. She counted
on you to see what she saw...

488
00:54:37,694 --> 00:54:40,572
...feel what she felt,
know what she knew.

489
00:54:40,947 --> 00:54:43,491
- What did she do, Angela?
- How should I know?

490
00:54:43,658 --> 00:54:45,952
- What did she do, Angela?
- I don't know.

491
00:54:47,287 --> 00:54:50,290
- What would you do?
- I don't know.

492
00:54:50,457 --> 00:54:55,003
What did she do, Angela? You know
what she did. What did she do, Angela?

493
00:54:55,170 --> 00:54:58,298
You know what she did. What are
you afraid of? What did she do?

494
00:54:58,465 --> 00:55:00,717
- What did she do?
- I don't know!

495
00:55:17,692 --> 00:55:19,778
When we were girls...

496
00:55:22,655 --> 00:55:25,367
...we would leave each other messages.

497
00:55:27,911 --> 00:55:29,704
In light.

498
00:55:32,248 --> 00:55:33,958
In breath.

499
00:55:38,046 --> 00:55:39,589
On the windows.

500
00:55:43,093 --> 00:55:46,888
John, there is no 17th act
in Corinthians.

501
00:55:49,057 --> 00:55:52,560
Corinthians goes to 21 acts
in the Bible in hell.

502
00:55:53,978 --> 00:55:55,772
They have Bibles in hell.

503
00:55:56,272 --> 00:55:58,650
Paints a different view of Revelations.

504
00:55:58,858 --> 00:56:00,860
Says the world will not end
by God's hand...

505
00:56:01,027 --> 00:56:03,905
...but be reborn in the embrace
of the damned.

506
00:56:04,072 --> 00:56:05,532
Though if you ask me...

507
00:56:06,199 --> 00:56:07,992
...fire's fire.

508
00:56:08,159 --> 00:56:12,247
16:29, 16:30.

509
00:56:12,497 --> 00:56:16,251
Oh, my, this is certainly not good.

